If the editor is opened with a malformed config file we shouldn't crash but
we _should_ display an error to the user in a new window explaining why we
had to fall back to the default config file.

-- config --
path: tests/data/config/malformed.toml
-- file-hello.txt --
-- buffer-list --
1      hello.txt
2    * +config-error
-- expected-windows --
1
2
-- expected-buffer-2 --
Unable to load config file:
malformed config file: TOML parse error at line 2, column 15
  |
2 | show_splash = "should be a bool"
  |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
invalid type: string "should be a bool", expected a boolean

